# Receipt archive tarballs: keep the extracted receipts, drop the archive.
receipts/**/*.tar.xz

# These two receipts sample the machine's live process/thermal/memory state
# (pid, cpu%, rss, competing_workloads) as their entire subject - that is what
# they are FOR, and their own test suites require the write to carry fresh
# live data every time (test_dirty_measure.py::test_entry_point_runs_and_seals_receipt,
# test_hcli_self_profile.py). Re-running the producer therefore never converges:
# a rerun changes pid/cpu/rss even when nothing the tool measures did, which is
# a live snapshot, not a fact that should be committed once and stay true.
# `git rm --cached` them once (see the wave report) - the doctrine that
# produces them stays in tools/future/*.py, tracked as source.
/receipts/future/DIRTY_MEASUREMENT.json
/receipts/future/HCLI_SELF_PROFILE.json

# --- Accidental shell redirections and runtime scratch (launch hardening) ---
# `none` is a multi-MB HF download log created by a stray `2>none`; `stdout` is
# the same mistake with an empty result. Neither is a deliverable.
/none
/stdout
